          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://get_ward_beds_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "get_ward_beds_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Step 1 of 2 to book a patient&#39;s follow-up visit. Pass the patient_id and a slot_id from get_followup_slots. The system checks that the discharge order asks for a follow-up, that the slot is open, of the right specialty and inside the follow-up window, and returns PROPOSED with a proposal_id and a summary (expires in 15 minutes), or BLOCKED with a reason_code and reason_text. Nothing is booked until confirm_action is called after the coordinator explicitly says yes to this exact summary. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "propose_followup",
            "handlerDescription": "Step 1 of 2 to book a patient's follow-up visit. Pass the patient_id and a slot_id from get_followup_slots. The system checks that the discharge order asks for a follow-up, that the slot is open, of the right specialty and inside the follow-up window, and returns PROPOSED with a proposal_id and a summary (expires in 15 minutes), or BLOCKED with a reason_code and reason_text. Nothing is booked until confirm_action is called after the coordinator explicitly says yes to this exact summary. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": false,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:propose_followup_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://propose_followup_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "propose_followup_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Step 2 of 2: book a follow-up the coordinator has explicitly confirmed. Pass the proposal_id from propose_followup. The system re-checks every rule and returns EXECUTED with a reference (e.g. BMC-APT-000101), or BLOCKED / EXPIRED (after 15 minutes) / NOT_FOUND / ALREADY_DONE with the reason. Only call after the coordinator says yes to the exact proposal. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "confirm_action",
            "handlerDescription": "Step 2 of 2: book a follow-up the coordinator has explicitly confirmed. Pass the proposal_id from propose_followup. The system re-checks every rule and returns EXECUTED with a reference (e.g. BMC-APT-000101), or BLOCKED / EXPIRED (after 15 minutes) / NOT_FOUND / ALREADY_DONE with the reason. Only call after the coordinator says yes to the exact proposal. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": false,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:confirm_action_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://confirm_action_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "confirm_action_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Order a patient&#39;s discharge medicines from the pharmacy. medication = ALL (or empty) for every medicine on the discharge list, or one or more names or codes (e.g. &#39;aspirin, metoprolol&#39;). Only medicines on the patient&#39;s discharge list can be ordered (anything else is NOT_ON_DISCHARGE_LIST), and only once the discharge order is signed. High-alert medicines (e.g. warfarin, oxycodone, enoxaparin, insulin) are not dispensed: the system parks them in a pharmacist case (PHARMACIST_REVIEW with case_id). pharmacist_brief = the medication reconciliation flags if a reconciliation was done, else empty; it is attached to any pharmacist case. Returns one row per medicine: ORDERED (order_id, pickup, ready_by), ALREADY_ORDERED, PHARMACIST_REVIEW, or BLOCKED with a reason. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "order_discharge_meds",
            "handlerDescription": "Order a patient's discharge medicines from the pharmacy. medication = ALL (or empty) for every medicine on the discharge list, or one or more names or codes (e.g. 'aspirin, metoprolol'). Only medicines on the patient's discharge list can be ordered (anything else is NOT_ON_DISCHARGE_LIST), and only once the discharge order is signed. High-alert medicines (e.g. warfarin, oxycodone, enoxaparin, insulin) are not dispensed: the system parks them in a pharmacist case (PHARMACIST_REVIEW with case_id). pharmacist_brief = the medication reconciliation flags if a reconciliation was done, else empty; it is attached to any pharmacist case. Returns one row per medicine: ORDERED (order_id, pickup, ready_by), ALREADY_ORDERED, PHARMACIST_REVIEW, or BLOCKED with a reason. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": false,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:order_discharge_meds_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://order_discharge_meds_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "order_discharge_meds_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Send a vacated bed on the coordinator&#39;s ward to housekeeping. Pass the bed_id (e.g. 4A-10). The system only accepts a bed whose patient has actually left (discharge_status DISCHARGED); it returns REQUESTED with a reference and the estimated ready time (45 minutes, or 90 for an isolation clean), or BLOCKED with PATIENT_NOT_DISCHARGED, ALREADY_REQUESTED, BED_EMPTY or NOT_FOUND. An early turnover while the patient is still on the unit needs the charge nurse (open_service_case bed_override). Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "request_bed_turnover",
            "handlerDescription": "Send a vacated bed on the coordinator's ward to housekeeping. Pass the bed_id (e.g. 4A-10). The system only accepts a bed whose patient has actually left (discharge_status DISCHARGED); it returns REQUESTED with a reference and the estimated ready time (45 minutes, or 90 for an isolation clean), or BLOCKED with PATIENT_NOT_DISCHARGED, ALREADY_REQUESTED, BED_EMPTY or NOT_FOUND. An early turnover while the patient is still on the unit needs the charge nurse (open_service_case bed_override). Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": false,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:request_bed_turnover_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://request_bed_turnover_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "request_bed_turnover_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Hand a request that needs a person to the right team. request_type is med_rec_review (agent_brief = the reconciliation flags), bed_override (early turnover while the patient is still on the unit; reference_id = the bed_id, or empty for the patient&#39;s bed), clinical_question (any dosage or clinical question), prescription_change (add, stop or change a medicine) or discharge_decision (whether or when the patient can go home). summary is a neutral 1-3 sentence summary in the coordinator&#39;s own words. The system routes it and returns OPENED with case_id, team and reply time, EXISTING, or BLOCKED / INVALID_TYPE with a reason. The assistant never answers clinical questions and never decides, promises or predicts the outcome. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "open_service_case",
            "handlerDescription": "Hand a request that needs a person to the right team. request_type is med_rec_review (agent_brief = the reconciliation flags), bed_override (early turnover while the patient is still on the unit; reference_id = the bed_id, or empty for the patient's bed), clinical_question (any dosage or clinical question), prescription_change (add, stop or change a medicine) or discharge_decision (whether or when the patient can go home). summary is a neutral 1-3 sentence summary in the coordinator's own words. The system routes it and returns OPENED with case_id, team and reply time, EXISTING, or BLOCKED / INVALID_TYPE with a reason. The assistant never answers clinical questions and never decides, promises or predicts the outcome. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": false,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:open_service_case_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://open_service_case_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "open_service_case_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "List the cases for patients on the coordinator&#39;s ward (requests a person decides): case_id, request, patient, what it is about, team, case_status (OPEN, APPROVED, REJECTED), opened and reply-due times, requested and approved days&#39; supply, and the customer_message from the reviewer once decided. Use it when the coordinator asks what happened to a request.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "get_my_cases",
            "handlerDescription": "List the cases for patients on the coordinator's ward (requests a person decides): case_id, request, patient, what it is about, team, case_status (OPEN, APPROVED, REJECTED), opened and reply-due times, requested and approved days' supply, and the customer_message from the reviewer once decided. Use it when the coordinator asks what happened to a request.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": true,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": true,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
